          "description": "Premium (0.02 RLUSD) — search or retrieve events from the Real-World Data Oracle. Covers four regulatory data feeds: sec_8k (8-K material events), sec_s1 (IPO filings), fda (FDA drug approvals), patents (USPTO patent grants). Returns machine-readable JSON events with timestamps, source URLs, and structured fields. Sub-second delivery vs Bloomberg's 5–10 minute lag — agents that catch the 8-K or FDA approval first win the trade. Pass feeds=[] to query all feeds. Pass keyword to text-search events. Pass since_ts (Unix timestamp) to get only recent events. Cost: 0.02 RLUSD per call. Pass payment_token from verify_payment.",
